Verdict: PASS. It's written to session_plan/eval_task_1.md.

• **The fix:** Multi-line edits on CRLF files now work. When `old_text` doesn't match the file as written but would match with each `\n` spelled `\r\n`, both old_text and new_text are rewritten that way. An exact match always takes priority, and line endings that are already \r\n are never doubled. The file is only read for multi-line old_text, and not at all above the existing size cap.
• **Tests:** I ran the 13 new tests and all pass. The key one edits `alpha\r\nbeta\r\ngamma\r\n` through the real `edit_file` tool and checks the result is exactly `ALPHA\r\nBETA\r\ngamma\r\n. The others cover a replacement with more lines and the cases that must stay unchanged: LF files, single-line edits, old_text already using \r\n`, and a mixed file.
• Error message: When an edit on a CRLF file still fails as not-found, one note about CRLF line endings is added to the error. It's added after the existing hint text, which is otherwise unchanged. On LF files the note is absent.
• **Nothing left unused:** every new function and the constant is called within the diff. `src/smart_edit.rs` is now 1977 lines, under the 2000-line cap, and no `NEUTERED` or DO NOT COMMIT marker remains.
• **Docs:** ARCHITECTURE.md has the new entry the task asked for. It covers the rule, the exact-match-first behaviour, the finding that yoagent does no line-ending handling, and the limit that old-Mac \r-only files aren't handled.
• **Product surface:** no config defaults, CLI flags, setup wizard or startup behaviour changed.
